&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SumUp | Product &amp;amp; Design | London, United Kingdom&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Competitive salary · Office-first&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role does not support Visa sponsorship and candidates must have the right to work in the UK.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Consumer Bank squad sits at the heart of one of SumUp&#39;s most exciting growth bets — scaling SumUp Pay, our consumer fintech product, to millions of active users across Europe. The team owns end-to-end UX and product design across the full user lifecycle, from onboarding and activation through to engagement features like Spaces, Open Banking insights, and budget tracking. This is a high-craft, high-autonomy environment where design isn&#39;t just execution — it&#39;s central to defining the problems worth solving, and your work will directly shape adoption, retention, and the future of SumUp&#39;s consumer offering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end product design within the Consumer Bank squad, from discovery through to delivery, across the SumUp Pay mobile experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead discovery by identifying user problems, framing opportunities, and shaping hypotheses alongside Product and Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design intuitive, high-quality mobile experiences in Figma that drive key metrics including activation, engagement, and retention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validate solutions through prototyping, user research, and usability testing, using both qualitative and quantitative data to iterate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the design system and help maintain consistency and quality across the product as SumUp scales its consumer offering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;You&#39;ll be great for this role if…&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience as a Senior Product Designer working on mobile-first consumer products, with a portfolio demonstrating end-to-end UX design and measurable impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong discovery skills, including problem framing, hypothesis definition, user research, and insight synthesis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent UX, interaction, and information design skills, with a high bar for quality and usability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working autonomously within cross-functional teams alongside Product Managers and Engineers, with solid understanding of technical constraints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to leverage AI design tools (e.g. for ideation, prototyping, and research synthesis) to accelerate workflows and elevate the quality of outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Figma and experience contributing to or evolving design systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why you should join SumUp&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌎 Opportunity to work with a truly global, multicultural team from our central London Bridge location. This involves an office-first setup&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌈 Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion: be part of a workplace that values and promotes diversity, fostering an inclusive environment where everyone&#39;s perspectives are respected and embraced&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🚀 Enrolment onto our Virtual Stock Option programme: you will own a stake in SumUp&#39;s future success&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏖️ Generous time off: enjoy 28 days of paid leave, plus bank holidays and special leaves&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏥 Health matters: private health insurance, including optical and dental&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🚗 Life made easier: salary-sacrifice commuter benefits via Gogeta&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💼 Financial security: retirement scheme (SumUp matches 7% when you contribute 5%)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🛡️ Peace of mind: life insurance from MetLife for 2× your salary&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌴 Break4me: 1-month sabbatical after 3 years of service&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🔗 Referral Bonus: earn additional rewards by referring talented individuals to join the SumUp team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About SumUp&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Be empowered to do more that matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At SumUp, we&#39;re on a mission to empower small businesses across the globe by providing simple and affordable tools that allow them to thrive. Today, over 4 million businesses in 37 markets rely on SumUp as their financial partner to manage payments, finance and customer relationships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our commitment to small businesses is reflected in &lt;a href=&quot;https://youtu.be/9DG64C3moeQ?si=YpcWuBNBTOQPzeLI&quot;&gt;our diverse team&lt;/a&gt; of over 3,000 SumUppers from over 90 nationalities, united by global collaboration and an innovative mindset. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.sumup.com/careers/culture/&quot;&gt;Our core values&lt;/a&gt; lay the foundation for who we are and what we stand for, shaping our work culture and driving our success. We foster inclusivity and a continuous learning culture, providing a safe space for personal and professional growth. Our differences make us unique and strong as we strive to create an environment where everyone belongs and feels supported, no matter how they identify.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SumUp is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, actively seeking and embracing diversity in our workforce. We don&#39;t make hiring or employment decisions based on race, colour, religion or religious belief, ethnic or national origin, nationality, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, age or any other basis protected by applicable laws or prohibited by company policy. Our commitment extends beyond recruitment to creating a safe and respectful workplace where harassment of any form is strictly prohibited. Discover more about our culture and opportunities on our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.sumup.com/careers/&quot;&gt;careers website&lt;/a&gt;, and follow our journey on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/sumup/&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/insidesumup/&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a -----
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🎬 Want to see more of life at SumUp? Explore our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sumup/Global-Employer-Brand-video-library-Empowering-Talent-Acquisition-partners-and-hiring-managers-194d3d97eb3c4eaca7ee2edff1a9d3fd&quot;&gt;Global Employer Brand video library&lt;/a&gt; to add to your job post or create LinkedIn posts.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Application Tip&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We recognise that candidates feel they need to meet 100% of the job criteria in order to apply for a job. Please note that this is only a guide. If you don’t tick every box, it’s ok too because it means you have room to learn and develop your career at SumUp.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Orcrist is building a next generation data intelligence platform using cutting-edge technologies. We&#39;re handling petabyte-scale data with sub-second queries. Our product is a Kubernetes‑based platform delivered as B2B SaaS or as a self‑hosted on‑prem solution, including air‑gapped deployments. We enable customers across defense, law enforcement, and enterprise to turn mission-critical data into actionable intelligence.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Every investigation starts with data. As PM for the Integration team, you make sure analysts in law enforcement and defense have the data they need, when they need it. You own the roadmap for integrating data from commercial vendors, open feeds, social media and messaging platforms, as well as the admin interfaces used to manage these integrations. Your work ensures data arrives current, traceable to its source and ready to use.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a largely technical PM role with significant ownership over a platform and admin experience that are still taking shape. You decide what gets built and in what order, working closely with engineers and other product teams to turn provider APIs and data models into scalable integrations and features that support analysts’ investigations. You’ll read API documentation, map provider data to OIP’s data model and write clear, actionable specs that engineers can build from.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the provider roadmap.&lt;/strong&gt; We add a source when it answers a question analysts can’t answer today, so you start from the analyst’s problem, not from a provider’s name. You talk regularly with analysts, admins and solutions engineers in law enforcement and defense, and with the upstream teams whose features bring integration requests. You decide which providers come next and what “done” means for each.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Write the technical specs.&lt;/strong&gt; Cover authentication, pagination, rate limits and quotas, incremental sync, deduplication, field mapping, and how failures surface. Every object must carry its provider, fetch time and source URL from the moment it is fetched. Our platform runs as SaaS and on-prem, so you also decide how each source behaves in each distribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the connectors as a product.&lt;/strong&gt; That covers the contract between connectors and the platform, versioning, and how quickly a new provider goes from evaluation to production. Every connector should make the next one cheaper. Where another team can reach a public source on its own, you give it a safe way to do so instead of putting it in our queue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the admin interfaces.&lt;/strong&gt; That means creating a connection, managing credentials, scheduling, health and status, logs, quota usage and permissions. A source we can’t monitor isn’t delivered, so every live connection needs a health check and clear failure states.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work with partnerships and legal.&lt;/strong&gt; You collaborate with the Director of OSINT and the Data Acquisition Manager to evaluate vendors, raise licensing and terms-of-service questions before we build, and turn the legal framework (storage, retention, redistribution) into product requirements. You also give the people negotiating contracts technical findings and cost per call.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage the teams around you.&lt;/strong&gt; Upstream, you work with the teams building user-facing features, such as graphs and maps, who bring integration requests from their intelligence domain. You help them find the analyst question behind each request and decide whether a shared connector can serve several of them. Downstream, you work with the foundation teams for ontology, machine learning and processing, so incoming data arrives in a shape they can use. You forecast the load of every high-volume source before it goes live.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape person-focused investigation tools.&lt;/strong&gt; You own how analysts go from a first lead about a person to a reviewed set of linked online identities. That includes how results are presented and reviewed, and how to avoid paying for the same lookup twice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measure the integration layer.&lt;/strong&gt; Track sync success rate, data freshness, time to onboard a provider, active connections, and time to resolve a failed connection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About you&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years as a Product Manager in B2B SaaS, with experience owning a technically complex area end-to-end, such as an integration platform, an API product, or data pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable in API documentation. You can discuss OAuth versus API keys, polling versus webhooks, pagination and rate limits with engineers as an equal, and you can try an endpoint yourself in Postman or curl.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have designed admin or configuration interfaces for technical users: connection setup, status and error states, audit trails.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You write specs and acceptance criteria that are specific enough to build and test against.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are data-fluent and define quality metrics for reliability and coverage, not just feature delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable with the legal side of third-party data: licensing, terms of service, GDPR, and provenance requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You work well across teams, since integrations touch engineering, partnerships, customer success, and every product that consumes the data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eligible to work in Germany and willing to travel to Berlin and across DACH for workshops and customer visits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Nice-to-haves&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have built or managed a connector framework, integration marketplace, or iPaaS product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with OSINT as a practitioner or product builder, and a sense of where existing collection tools fall short.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Kubernetes, on-prem, or air-gapped deployment constraints and what they mean for integration architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with entity resolution or link analysis, and how ingested data feeds them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;German language (B1+)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with law enforcement or defense users in Germany or the DACH region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we offer&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 [&amp;quot;list&amp;quot;,{&amp;quot;spread&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;start&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;end&amp;quot;:273},&amp;quot;regular_list_item&amp;quot;,{&amp;quot;start&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;end&amp;quot;:273}]&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Real ownership, real impact:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Own a critical layer of the platform that every customer relies on. Much of the integration platform and its admin experience is still taking shape, so you identify the problems, set priorities, decide what gets built, and see it through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remote-first, Germany-wide: &lt;/strong&gt;Work from wherever you do your best work, with regular team gatherings in Berlin and other off-site locations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexibility by default: &lt;/strong&gt;Flexible working hours help you make work fit your life.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your setup, your way: &lt;/strong&gt;Get a personal home-office equipment budget to create a workspace that works for you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;30 days of vacation:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Take the time you need to recharge and come back with fresh energy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Keep growing: &lt;/strong&gt;We invest in your personal and professional development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Get rewarded for impact: &lt;/strong&gt;Performance bonuses are tied to agreed objectives and key results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A warm welcome: &lt;/strong&gt;Every new team member gets a welcome goodie bag.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Good people, good times: &lt;/strong&gt;From summer and Christmas parties to regular team gatherings, we make time to celebrate together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A mission that matters: &lt;/strong&gt;Work on challenges with tangible impact on public safety and national security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Global Structure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Deliveroo is now part of DoorDash, bringing together teams with even greater reach, scale, and ambition. Depending on your role, you may collaborate with teammates, systems, and leaders across DoorDash and Wolt. Together, we’re unlocking new possibilities as one global team.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the Team&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Our Trust &amp;amp; Safety, Integrity and Fraud Product team is dedicated to ensuring a safe and trusted experience for all customers across our platform, including Consumers, Merchants, and Couriers. We tackle complex challenges, from preventing fraud, abuse and Account Takeover to ensuring authenticity, to building regulatory compliance capabilities, all while balancing risk mitigation and providing a seamless user experience. Our team partners closely with cross-functional groups, including Engineering, Data Science, Compliance, and Risk Operations, to drive strategic initiatives that protect our business while fostering growth.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h1&gt;About the Role&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Trust is foundational to an on-demand marketplace. Deliveroo, DoorDash and Wolt are converging European capabilities into one platform and one global product capability to prevent fraud and abuse. The marketplace is expanding rapidly beyond just restaurants as we become “your door to more.&quot; As we add new products, geographies, ways for Consumers, Merchants and Couriers to engage, we’re expanding and enhancing our fraud capabilities to be best in the industry at keeping our platform safe and trustworthy. We strongly believe that trust is the most important attribute of an online marketplace, and the team ensures that we maintain this trust.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Senior Product Manager that will lead dedicated cross-functional teams to solve complex challenges that impact Consumers, Couriers and Merchants and touch every corner of our business - from new user onboarding, to the in-app delivery experience, to the products and services being created that our users can’t find anywhere else. We are looking to hire for a few roles, so you’ll either lead a vertical fraud team protecting Consumers, Couriers or Merchants, or lead a horizontal fraud platform team focused on building our Risk Engine, Data Signals Intelligence and Automation / Anomaly Detection capabilities or leading compliance and authenticity efforts involving Identity Verification and Right to Work. The Fraud team is in hyper growth in terms of its size and impact and offers a unique opportunity to set and execute on a vision that will shape the future of Deliveroo, DoorDash and Wolt globally.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h1&gt;You’re excited about this opportunity because you will…&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Set the vision and long-term product strategy for one of our vertical fraud teams or our horizontal platform fraud team.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Prevent, detect and mitigate fraud and abuse, building and leveraging AI systems to address risk in real time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Build an AI-led fraud operations platform that turns complex marketplace signals into automated decisions, prioritised investigations, and actionable case workflows, stopping fraud, abuse and manipulation before incidents occur.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Develop and execute a customer-focused product roadmap through close collaboration with senior leadership, Operations, Data Science, Analytics, Design, and Engineering all while balancing business needs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Translate customer and internal-user needs into clear, well-defined functional and technical requirements backed by data analysis and deep understanding of our users&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Guide and interface closely with data analysis and engineering teams to define scope, review and refine technical capabilities, prioritize projects for release, and define new opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Build long-term instrumentation, monitoring, and evaluation capabilities for product performance, tracking, and to create product insights.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Establish business cases and projected return on investment to identify and prioritize opportunities&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Partner with Finance and Business Leaders to manage the impact on the profitability of the overall business.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Establish success metrics and executive reviews covering fraud trends and P&amp;amp;L impact.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h1&gt;We’re excited about you because you have…&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;5+ years of product management experience, with a track record of owning complex, cross-functional products from strategy through execution in ambiguous problem spaces.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Experience defining strategic vision and roadmap execution in a given product area.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Demonstrated experience shipping AI-enabled or automation-heavy products, with sound judgment about where models can accelerate decisions and where human expertise, safeguards, and accountability must remain central.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Experience in technology, fraud, privacy, security, data governance, trust &amp;amp; safety, risk or an enthusiasm to learn and keep customers and the ecosystem fraud-free and protected&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Strong ability to translate ambiguous policy, legal, or regulatory requirements into practical, scalable product solutions and clear engineering priorities.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fluency in modern AI product development, including evaluating model quality, designing human-in-the-loop experiences, and translating emerging capabilities into practical, measurable customer and business value.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Extreme customer centricity with a focus on ensuring low-friction experiences for good customers.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;An analytical, structured approach to ambiguity and risk, with the ability to frame tradeoffs, define controls, and set measurable outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Experience partnering effectively with Legal, Compliance, Public Policy, Security, Privacy, Operations, Data Science, Design, and Engineering.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;An interest in applying AI and data-driven systems to improve fraud detection, triage, escalation, and prevention, with sound judgment about safeguards and human oversight.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Excellent communication and stakeholder-management skills, including the ability to align senior leaders around urgent, high-stakes decisions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Direct experience applying AI/ML to prevent, prevent, detect and mitigate harm, plus AI fluency — you can build a feature with AI – not just write PRDs.Why Join Us?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Why Join Us?&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Deliveroo, you’ll do work that matters, solving real-world problems in a three-sided marketplace that’s constantly evolving.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;We’re food lovers, problem solvers, community builders and more, brought together by a shared drive to make things better. Working here you can expect to:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;🔧 &lt;strong&gt;Solve meaningful problems at real scale&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Work on a complex, always-on marketplace that impacts millions every day.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;🌱 &lt;strong&gt;See your impact, fast&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ship, test and improve ideas quickly in a low-hierarchy, high-ownership environment.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;🧠 &lt;strong&gt;Grow through challenge and ownership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Take on big, ambiguous problems and accelerate your career with strong support.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;🌎 &lt;strong&gt;A culture built for builders&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;High standards, collaboration, flexible working and continuous learning.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;💰 &lt;strong&gt;Share in the success you help create&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Competitive salary and equity options, so you’re rewarded for the impact you make.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;➡️ Want a deeper look at how we build? Check out our &lt;a target=&quot;_blank&quot; class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot; href=&quot;deliveroo.engineering&quot;&gt;Tech Blog&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;We aim to create a fair process that lets your skills shine—our interview typically includes 3-4 stages. Find more about how we hire &lt;a target=&quot;_blank&quot; class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot; href=&quot;https://careers.deliveroo.co.uk/how-we-hire/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Our Global Structure&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Deliveroo is now part of DoorDash, bringing together teams with even greater reach, scale, and ambition. Depending on your role, you may collaborate with teammates, systems, and leaders across DoorDash and Wolt. Together, we’re unlocking new possibilities as one global team.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Diversity, Equity and Inclusion&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Deliveroo, we know that a great workplace reflects the world around us and that true diversity and inclusion make us stronger, more creative, and better at what we do. We’re committed to fostering an environment where everyone can do their best work and feel they belong.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;We believe in equality of opportunity and welcome candidates from all backgrounds regardless of age, gender, ethnicity, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, socio-economic background, religion, or belief.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;If you have a disability or long-term health condition and need support to apply for one of our roles, or require any reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process, you’ll have the opportunity to let us know once you’ve submitted your application. We’ll share details on how to request support so we can ensure you have a fair and equitable experience.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;If you’re excited about making a real impact in a fast-moving marketplace and growing your career alongside ambitious, supportive teams, we’d love to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity, Equity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;At Deliveroo, we know that a great workplace reflects the world around us and that true diversity and inclusion make us stronger, more creative, and better at what we do. We’re committed to fostering an environment where everyone can do their best work and feel they belong.&lt;/p&gt;
